prtg-network-monitoring is the PRTG Network Monitor (Paessler) configuration, operations, and tuning skill:
the sensor-based monitoring model and sensor-count optimisation, licensing tiers, auto-discovery and device
templates, the sensor catalogue (SNMP/WMI/flow/HTTP/custom), on-premises core-plus-probe architecture vs
PRTG Hosted Monitor SaaS, remote probe design, maps/dashboards/reports, notifications and escalation, and
the HTTP API. It is a vendor ops skill in the NMS family; the DESIGN/paradigm/platform-selection decision
lives in network-monitoring-selection (PR 1), to which this skill routes the design question back.
Skill licensed MIT (the primary-source licence).

Part of NMS family PR 2 of 3 (PRTG + Kentik, MIT single-source). Scope = full ops per the DNS +
Load-balancer precedent.

